coin_nodemcu.bin is a compiled ESP8266 (NodeMCU) firmware image. It combines
the project's own sketch with third-party code, so it is NOT licensed under
the project's AGPLv3 alone:

  project's own sketch   hotspot/nodemcucodeholder (coin_nodemcu.ino)
                         SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

  third-party code linked into the image (from the ESP8266 Arduino core
  toolchain it is built with):
    ESP8266 Arduino core and its bundled libraries (e.g. ESP8266HTTPClient)
        LGPL-2.1-or-later     https://github.com/esp8266/Arduino
    LittleFS (littlefs)
        BSD-3-Clause          https://github.com/littlefs-project/littlefs
    lwIP
        BSD-3-Clause          https://savannah.nongnu.org/projects/lwip/
    Espressif ESP8266 NONOS SDK precompiled libraries
        Espressif's own terms https://github.com/espressif/ESP8266_NONOS_SDK

This NOTICE stands in for a source-file header (the artifact is a compiled
binary and cannot carry one). The licenses of the individual third-party
files vary; consult the upstream projects at the versions used for the build.

LGPL-2.1 relinking: the complete sketch source is in this repository
(hotspot/nodemcucodeholder), so the image can be rebuilt against a modified
copy of the core or its libraries. The full LGPL-2.1 text is in
LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt of the source repository.
